{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question","id":972274,"title":"Odd frenzy question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-18T19:11:42-07:00","id":972274,"title":"Odd frenzy question","content":"In the Blood and Smoke book, one of the ghoul merits is Beast Whispers. Allowing the ghoul to act as a Touchstone for Kindred.<br /> The Rules allow a touchstone to attempt to talk down a frenzied vampire with an extended social action.<br /> If a ghoul had majesty 2 thus would get 2 extra dice to presence rolls would this help in calming down a frenzied vampire?<br /> <br /> What about dominate? Would dominate be allowed as part of the Social roll to stop a frenzy?<br /> <br /> Normally social and discipline rolls fail to stop a frenzied vampire, but this is an odd exception.<br /> How would this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T02:12:02-07:00","id":972413,"title":"","content":"I would rule no but people constantly find rules I've missed so it might be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T03:21:52-07:00","id":972432,"title":"","content":"Normally only someone who is a touchstone to a specific kindred may talk that kindred (and only that kindred) out of frenzy on an extended social roll which takes into account the kindred's blood potency. With the merit they can potentially talk any kindred from frenzy, not just the one for whom they're a touchstone. The merit doesn't let ghoul touchstones add their discipline rating to use powers against kindred and attempts to Dominate the kindred out of frenzy would still auto-fail. (You aren't talking them out of frenzy you're trying to instantly force them to obey you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:57:46-07:00","id":972620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=972432#post972432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally only someone who is a touchstone to a specific kindred may talk that kindred (and only that kindred) out of frenzy on an extended social roll which takes into account the kindred's blood potency. With the merit they can potentially talk any kindred from frenzy, not just the one for whom they're a touchstone. The merit doesn't let ghoul touchstones add their discipline rating to use powers against kindred and attempts to Dominate the kindred out of frenzy would still auto-fail. (You aren't talking them out of frenzy you're trying to instantly force them to obey you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <br /> Majesty would give you the +2 to your social roll which you are rolling to talk the vampire out of the frenzy, so yes I would allow that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:48:00-07:00","id":972659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=972620#post972620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed<br /> <br /> Majesty would give you the +2 to your social roll which you are rolling to talk the vampire out of the frenzy, so yes I would allow that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would probably roll this way as well. However, I could see a case being made that because Awe can be cancelled by a beast lashing out, that it has no effect on a Kindred fully frenzied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:55:42-07:00","id":972791,"title":"","content":"Well the reason I was asking is because yes the rules say mental disciplines and social rolls normally automatically fail. <br /> <br /> The touchstone is the only one that has a chance to talk someone down with social rolls. <br /> <br /> However it also says you can redirect a frenzied vampire with mental disciplines. While very dangerous I was thinking it would make sense that by forcing the frenzied vampire to focus on you it would help in the social roll.<br /> <br /> Just obviously barring him succeeding in one roll or someone savings said ghoul he would likely be the sole focus of the frenzied kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:53:15-07:00","id":972826,"title":"","content":"Disciplines can situationally redirect the target of frenzy, not end frenzy. That's a relevant distintion. If you're the only viable target or the cause, you aren't redirecting frenzy.<br /> <br /> I tend to picture a touchstone talking someone out of frenzy by trying to convince them that ripping someone to shreds, burning someone's car etc. is not the best idea while the vampire is splintering a bat into a stake or pouring kerosene. In one instance, the touchstone went into lurid detail, of a more heinous form of destruction was better revenge but had to be planned out first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:15:38-07:00","id":972853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=972659#post972659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would probably roll this way as well. However, I could see a case being made that because Awe can be cancelled by a beast lashing out, that it has no effect on a Kindred fully frenzied.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well.. Yes. But you would have to lash out to make it stop. Just because something CAN be canceled doesnt mean it doesnt work. It stops working when it is canceled out.. not before. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=972791#post972791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the reason I was asking is because yes the rules say mental disciplines and social rolls normally automatically fail.<br /> <br /> The touchstone is the only one that has a chance to talk someone down with social rolls.<br /> <br /> However it also says you can redirect a frenzied vampire with mental disciplines. While very dangerous I was thinking it would make sense that by forcing the frenzied vampire to focus on you it would help in the social roll.<br /> <br /> Just obviously barring him succeeding in one roll or someone savings said ghoul he would likely be the sole focus of the frenzied kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can redirect targets but not objectives. If they were in a Kill frenzy, you might not want to redirect that to you with a Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:49:35-07:00","id":972868,"title":"","content":"Right. I'm not saying it's a good idea to make yourself a target, far from it. <br /> <br /> But I've been trying to point out the fact that a touchstone can actually make a social roll to calm down a kindred in frenzy where it would normally fail for everybody else. <br /> <br /> Anybody can use a discipline to attempt to redirect a kindred. That's nothing special. <br /> <br /> So the question is would this intimate connection between touchstone and kindred allow them to break through with a discipline?<br /> <br /> If it's just forcing them to face the touchstone that the kindred themselves don't want to destroy, majesty.<br /> <br /> Or showing that kindred just what a monster they are becoming, nightmare. <br /> <br /> Or standing in defiance. Demanding they calm down or destroy something they value, dominate. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying it should be a flat success.<br /> <br /> I'm saying maybe bonus dice, with a high probability that a failure at any point be treated like a dramatic failure. <br /> <br /> This is of course a really weird situation. Normally a touchstone wouldn't have disciplines. But the beast whispers merit makes it possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:38:49-07:00","id":973062,"title":"","content":"This isn't really covered in the rules, so I'd say you have to decide what 'Talking Down' is in a thematic sense.<br /> <br /> For me - Touchstones are a deliberate connection of a character's Man side of the Man/Beast pair to Humanity. Touchstones are a tangible reminder/example of what is human. This gives touchstones a special ability to reach through the ravings of the Beast and allow the Man to come back into control as a guide away from the beast.<br /> <br /> Going with that theme, I would consider Disciplines in ghouls a manifestation of the Beast, not a manifestation of what makes Touchstones human. Disciplines would actually detract from the essence of humanity. I would say that the frenzying Beast would process another Beast in that and actually respond like a fellow predator - sticking with the Feed/Fight/Flee trio. If the discipline is something that adds a passive effect to the Touchstone's stats - Applicable to a talking-down Social Roll - I would let that fly. But if the effect attempts to alter/control the frenzying Kindred, I'd auto-fail it.<br /> <br /> If, however, you see Touchstones gaining their special connection with Kindred as something inherently 'them' - a personal relationship where they have a back door during frenzy - I could see it making sense that Disciplines can go through that back door.<br /> <br /> I personally think RAW lends itself more to the former, but the example isn't specifically laid out in the books as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:27:53-07:00","id":973088,"title":"","content":"I'm agree with Holy. The point of being able to talk a vampire down is to appeal to their human side (dare I say, to Anchor the vampires?) and to reject the Beast. Disciplines, by nature, aren't appeals, they're coercion. They're direct and forceful. The Beast shrugs off that kind of attempt. There's a reason that Disciplines generally bypass the Social Maneuvering system in the first place - the targets don't get a choice in the matter. Social Maneuver targets do.<br /> <br /> I don't really have a problem with giving dice bonuses from Majesty or Nightmare, because its hard enough already, and getting 3xBP Doors open is not easy. Especially not with how high BP gets in games now, and that you're on a clock until the vamp loses it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:51:54-07:00","id":973189,"title":"","content":"I think that it is pretty well covered in the Book.<br /> <br /> Awe gives +Majesty to presence rolls. Not &quot;in some cases&quot;, but in ALL cases that Awe is active. therefore, if it is active ( and not shut down with a lashing out ), you get the bonus.<br /> <br /> Touchstones are allowed to make an extended social roll to talk the vampire down from a frenzy. Social roll would likely be Presence + Persuasion ( Awe, striking looks and skill specialties all apply ) <br /> <br /> <br /> A direct attempt on ending the frenzy through a discipline auto fails. A direct attempt to do something to a vampire when you are a ghoul autofails, Such as Dominate or Charm. Awe does not directly influence anything external. It Internally changes you. It indirectly does because it only allows the user a dice bonus to their direct attempts, Striking looks or a skill specialty would. <br /> <br /> A frenzied vampire does not flat out ignore the beasts. No where does it say that a frenzied vampire is immune to disciplines. It actually says you can use them on a vampire who is frenzied. You can dominate a frenzied vampire, you cant end their frenzy, but you can change their targets. You can charm a frenzied vampire to perhaps not eat you, but someone else.<br /> <br /> Awe and majesty is so very subtle that no one knows they were ever effected by it. It even says that vampires dont know you are using it and dont ever feel cheated after. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:11:06-07:00","id":973207,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that Ghouls using Disciplines on Vampires do not get to use their Discipline rating if it is contested or resisted. Auto-fail only happens if they have any stage of Blood-Bonding to the target.<br /> <br /> Talking someone down from Frenzy also seems more like Manipulation than Presence (I'm not sure how much charisma and authority one can conjure up as a Ghoul or Human against a Frenzying Vampire), but I admit that strongly depends on both your Storyteller and your attempted method.<br /> <br /> Personally, I see the exception being made for Social rolls. I see nothing in the text that indicates an exception for Disciplines. Using Disciplines to coerce a vampire into ending their Frenzy fails. A Frenzying Beast can't be swayed by another Beast. Only the Man, which is what a Touchstone petitions with their social roll. That's how I'd justify it in-character.<br /> <br /> Though I don't really think allowing the bonus from Awe (and not any other Disciplines or Majesty abilities) would break things or be too much of a stretch. But I definitely wouldn't allow anything else to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:27:34-07:00","id":973216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973189#post973189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( Awe, striking looks and skill specialties all apply )</div> </div> </div> </div>Why on earth would being pretty help you talk down a vampire about to frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:06:29-07:00","id":973279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973216#post973216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why on earth would being pretty help you talk down a vampire about to frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;T'was beauty killed the beast.&quot;<br /> <br /> But seriously, Striking Looks in 2E is no longer just &quot;pretty&quot; - it's any type of physical appearance / social aura that makes you more striking for a variety of reasons. That 'striking light' may be better as a beacon for cutting through the blood-red rage of a frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:21:02-07:00","id":973286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973216#post973216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why on earth would being pretty help you talk down a vampire about to frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't. Unless your ST thinks whoring yourself to a frenzied vampire is a valid extended social action to get a vampire out of frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:29:09-07:00","id":973292,"title":"","content":"I probably wouldn't allow Striking Looks to apply, regardless of what form the ghoul's or touchstone's striking appearance takes. Everyone looks like lunch to a Frenzying vampire.<br /> <br /> Awe would totally apply on a Presence based roll though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:59:25-07:00","id":973372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973292#post973292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably wouldn't allow Striking Looks to apply, regardless of what form the ghoul's or touchstone's striking appearance takes. Everyone looks like lunch to a Frenzying vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to Disagree here. I think Striking Looks and/or physical appearance in general could easily be a discerning factor in determining beast's desires. Trying to decide which prey is the most appealing, which threat is the most dangerous, which rival presents the greatest challenge - there can be a lot of physical cues from how someone looks in any of those choices. Saying a frenzying Kindred fundamentally ignores all physical cues - that all prey looks the same - I don't think is supported.<br /> <br /> There are other factors too - who's closer, kindred vs. human vs. animal, blood potency - but I wouldn't flatly discount the purely visual ones.<br /> <br /> That being said, I would play it both ways. Striking Looks might make you more a target of frenzy in some cases, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:15:45-07:00","id":973383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973216#post973216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why on earth would being pretty help you talk down a vampire about to frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot; </i>Effect: Your character is stunning, alarming, <b>commanding</b>,<br /> repulsing, threatening, <b>charming</b>, or<b> otherwise worthy of<br /> attention</b>. Determine how your character looks and how people<br /> react to that. <i>For one dot, your character gets a +1 die bonus on<br /> any Social rolls that would be influenced by his looks. For two<br /> dots, the benefit increases to +2. Depending on the particulars,<br /> this might influence Expression, Intimidation, Persuasion,<br /> Subterfuge, or other rolls. &quot; </i><br /> <br /> Whether or not Striking Looks allows you to influence people by giving a bonus to social rolls.... It's right there as RAW.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#003399\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cI would sooner destroy a stained glass window as an artist like yourself. However, since I can't have you following me either.\u201d&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> I assume that it could mean ( in this context ) that you believe your touchstone to be a beautiful thing and you would not want to destroy something so beautiful. Or perhaps the beauty distracts you from your rage even if it is momentarily. Or like Holy said it isnt just &quot;pretty&quot; it is a lot of things. But again as RAW it's right there. it gives you +1 or 2 on social rolls.. Talking down a vampire is a social roll. That pretty much should end the debate right there.<br /> <br /> Also just because your looks are striking doesnt mean you are &quot;whoring yourself&quot; I think that is a pretty big leap there. It could be the thing of beauty or hope in all that blood soaked mess.<br /> Getting your frenzied vampire to notice you with awe is almost the same thing as getting a vampire to notice you by using your looks... They are both bolstering Presence rolls.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For better or worse: It is a proven fact that people are more likely to get what they want based on their looks. Thousands of studies have been done on this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:31:08-07:00","id":973480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973292#post973292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably wouldn't allow Striking Looks to apply, regardless of what form the ghoul's or touchstone's striking appearance takes. Everyone looks like lunch to a Frenzying vampire.<br /> <br /> Awe would totally apply on a Presence based roll though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone looks like lunch yes. But I assume the point of touchstones was that they effect the man inside the beast.<br /> <br /> I could see a particularly smitten deva that would prefer jump into a bonfire than hurt their pretty.. and they would throw every piece of willpower they had to stop from killing them. <br /> <br /> The matter of striking looks I would see as situational. Just as disciplines in this really odd delimma","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:21:47-07:00","id":973677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973383#post973383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>&quot; </i>Effect: Your character is stunning, alarming, <b>commanding</b>,<br /> repulsing, threatening, <b>charming</b>, or<b> otherwise worthy of<br /> attention</b>. Determine how your character looks and how people<br /> react to that. <i>For one dot, your character gets a +1 die bonus on<br /> any Social rolls that would be influenced by his looks. For two<br /> dots, the benefit increases to +2. Depending on the particulars,<br /> this might influence Expression, Intimidation, Persuasion,<br /> Subterfuge, or other rolls. &quot; </i><br /> <br /> Whether or not Striking Looks allows you to influence people by giving a bonus to social rolls.... It's right there as RAW.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#003399\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cI would sooner destroy a stained glass window as an artist like yourself. However, since I can't have you following me either.\u201d&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> I assume that it could mean ( in this context ) that you believe your touchstone to be a beautiful thing and you would not want to destroy something so beautiful. Or perhaps the beauty distracts you from your rage even if it is momentarily. Or like Holy said it isnt just &quot;pretty&quot; it is a lot of things. But again as RAW it's right there. it gives you +1 or 2 on social rolls.. Talking down a vampire is a social roll. That pretty much should end the debate right there.<br /> <br /> Also just because your looks are striking doesnt mean you are &quot;whoring yourself&quot; I think that is a pretty big leap there. It could be the thing of beauty or hope in all that blood soaked mess.<br /> Getting your frenzied vampire to notice you with awe is almost the same thing as getting a vampire to notice you by using your looks... They are both bolstering Presence rolls.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For better or worse: It is a proven fact that people are more likely to get what they want based on their looks. Thousands of studies have been done on this...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not sure how I'd handle it if it came up, but this is a very strong argument in favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T01:34:39-07:00","id":973719,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think the Striking Looks thing comes down to who they are to the PC. That cute girl from high school gets to use hers because it's part of who she is to you while your hot sister does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:01:41-07:00","id":973786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973719#post973719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think the Striking Looks thing comes down to who they are to the PC. That cute girl from high school gets to use hers because it's part of who she is to you while your hot sister does not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"http://bm23tvreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/got-cersei.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:26:16-07:00","id":973806,"title":"","content":"Anomalys exist.<br /> Fucked up Ventrue anomalys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:34:31-07:00","id":973811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973719#post973719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think the Striking Looks thing comes down to who they are to the PC. That cute girl from high school gets to use hers because it's part of who she is to you while your hot sister does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy made a good point there with that picture. But even your &quot;Hot sister&quot; As grown accustomed to her looks and knows how to persuade people better based on the reactions of other people. Striking looks is not like awe in the sense where you can turn it on or off. It becomes part of who you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:35:30-07:00","id":974262,"title":"","content":"It also depends on the type of Striking Looks they're wielding, I suppose. A person with a Striking Looks that is described as innocent, trustworthy, and endearing could certainly apply in a situation that's about calming a Vampire down. But only in the context that looking innocent helps bolster their attempts to persuade the Vampire logically.<br /> <br /> For example, a character with Striking Looks (Scary as Fuck) shouldn't get the bonus if they're trying to sweet-talk the Vampire into calming down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T03:47:20-07:00","id":974326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=973786#post973786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://bm23tvreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/got-cersei.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Well this brother wasn't that impressed with her looks.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=440\" data-tempid=\"temp_440_1474541212307_881\" /><br /> <br /> And I can name eight others who weren't swayed by her appearance either.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-22-2016, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:31:17-07:00","id":974370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974326#post974326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well this brother wasn't that impressed with her looks.<br /> <br /> And I can name eight others who weren't swayed by her appearance either.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the image is Tyrion. And this is getting pretty deep down the rabbit hole of this tangent, but...<br /> <br /> It's still only a +1/+2. Rolls fail, and other modifiers (like a lifetime of contempt) certainly can add way more penalties than a Striking Looks bonus to any given roll. I'm certainly not making the argument that people with Striking Looks can never make enemies and always get what they want.<br /> <br /> I'm saying it makes it a little easier to get what you want, when - as Jack mentioned above - the types of looks apply to the situation. <br /> <br /> Dad is going to be a little more likely to believe his daughter with 'Striking Looks: Innocent' didn't steal the cash out of his wallet than the daughter without the Merit. <br /> Tywin is going to maybe be a little more partial to his two kids with 'Striking Looks: Regal Presence' than the son without.<br /> <br /> And here's the weird creeper question, but...<br /> <br /> Are you saying that if two adult sisters were Dominated to seduce their father by a Ventrue Acolyte with an Oedipus complex as part of some out-there blood ritual, you wouldn't let the daughter with 'Striking Looks: Seductive/Pretty' apply a bonus to her roll? I would apply a 'close family' penalty to both rolls assuming the game is in a culture where those types of relationships aren't normal (modern), but I wouldn't discount the Merit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:47:12-07:00","id":974376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974370#post974370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Striking Looks: Innocent</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, I think, a point where people are going to differ on what Striking Looks can or can't do. To me, &quot;Innocent&quot; is too subjective to be a Striking Looks quality. You can have Striking Looks: youthful face, and some people will be more inclined to assume your innocence, but others might not. You can have Striking Looks: heavily modded, and some people might be intimidated by that while others might be turned on. In my opinion, Striking Looks should determine physical qualities, and different characters should react to those qualities in different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:54:33-07:00","id":974382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974376#post974376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, I think, a point where people are going to differ on what Striking Looks can or can't do. To me, &quot;Innocent&quot; is too subjective to be a Striking Looks quality. You can have Striking Looks: youthful face, and some people will be more inclined to assume your innocence, but others might not. You can have Striking Looks: nasty scar, and some people might be intimidated by that while others might be turned on. In my opinion, Striking Looks should determine physical qualities, and different characters should react to those qualities in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Effect: Your character is stunning, alarming, commanding, repulsing, threatening, charming, or otherwise worthy of attention. </div> </div> </div>All of these are subjective and are the direct book examples under the merit description. I think 2E moved toward a more subjective mechanic than the old 1E mechanic. It no longer specifically calls out a directly physical component - I would say much like the Nosferatu Flaw switched from oWoD to nWod from physical appearance to a general social penalty which CAN include physical appearance.<br /> <br /> But you are correct that it's situational:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on the particulars, this might influence Expression, Intimidation, Persuasion, Subterfuge, or other rolls. </div> </div> </div>If you are using any of the above skills during a talking down (or any other) roll, then Striking Looks might apply.<br /> <br /> Edit: But totally, if your game decides that Striking Looks is a purely physical attribute like a Scar or Youthful Face, AND you play that the beast doesn't notice those kinds of nuances - then you are totally justified in saying a Striking Looks bonus doesn't apply to the talking-down roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 09-22-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:06:31-07:00","id":974387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974382#post974382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these are subjective and are the direct book examples under the merit description. I think 2E moved toward a more subjective mechanic than the old 1E mechanic. It no longer specifically calls out a directly physical component - I would say much like the Nosferatu Flaw switched from oWoD to nWod from physical appearance to a general social penalty which CAN include physical appearance.<br /> <br /> But you are correct that it's situational:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you are using any of the above skills during a talking down (or any other) roll, then Striking Looks might apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes someone look &quot;stunning, alarming, commanding, repulsing, threatening, charming, or otherwise worthy of attention&quot; is naturally going to vary from one observer to the next. The very next sentence in the Merit description says &quot;Determine how your character looks and how people react to that.&quot; In my interpretation, &quot;how your character looks&quot; refers to physical qualities like a chiseled jaw or shifty eyes, and &quot;how people react to that&quot; should be different for different people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:17:27-07:00","id":974393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974387#post974387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes someone look &quot;stunning, alarming, commanding, repulsing, threatening, charming, or otherwise worthy of attention&quot; is naturally going to vary from one observer to the next. The very next sentence in the Merit description says &quot;Determine how your character looks and how people react to that.&quot; In my interpretation, &quot;how people react to that&quot; is different for different people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is definitely true, and a fair way to run things.<br /> <br /> For me, I tend to let the players dictate when they think their looks would apply, and rarely override them. It lets me avoid putting brainpower into deciding which NPCs think scars are sexy and which don't. So I let people choose their 'specialty' as it were, and subjective ones are fine with me.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the discussion, and sorry if I sounded snippy - haven't had my caffeine yet. : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:23:40-07:00","id":974399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974393#post974393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is definitely true, and a fair way to run things.<br /> <br /> For me, I tend to let the players dictate when they think their looks would apply, and rarely override them. It lets me avoid putting brainpower into deciding which NPCs think scars are sexy and which don't. So I let people choose their 'specialty' as it were, and subjective ones are fine with me.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the discussion, and sorry if I sounded snippy - haven't had my caffeine yet. : )</div> </div> </div> </div>You're good, no worries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think your interpretation is perfectly valid as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:53:22-07:00","id":974414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974382#post974382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All of these are subjective and are the direct book examples under the merit description. I think 2E moved toward a more subjective mechanic than the old 1E mechanic. It no longer specifically calls out a directly physical component - I would say much like the Nosferatu Flaw switched from oWoD to nWod from physical appearance to a general social penalty which CAN include physical appearance.<br /> <br /> But you are correct that it's situational:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you are using any of the above skills during a talking down (or any other) roll, then Striking Looks might apply.<br /> <br /> Edit: But totally, if your game decides that Striking Looks is a purely physical attribute like a Scar or Youthful Face, AND you play that the beast doesn't notice those kinds of nuances - then you are totally justified in saying a Striking Looks bonus doesn't apply to the talking-down roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A good read: <a href=\"http://www.newsweek.com/beauty-advantage-how-looks-affect-your-work-your-career-your-life-74313\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newsweek.com/beauty-advan...our-life-74313</a> <br /> good looking people make 4-5% more per year than the average joe... I would say that is a +1/+2 Bonus to their social rolls. <br /> <br /> But seriously guys. We are arguing about whether or not you should get a +1 or 2 bonus on your social rolls due to your looks? If you say that you cant get that bonus, what would the point of taking the merit be? Even the gay guy could be more easily persuaded by the pretty woman. it isnt about whether or not you are sexually attracted to them, it's about psychology saying that as people ( and vampires were people ) are more likely to listen to something we find visually appealing. More likely to consider their point of view, more likely to let them finish their thoughts. We might not be sexually attracted to Brad Pitt, but we could all agree that he is a good looking man. Does that mean we want to do him? no. It just means he is easy on the eyes and if he had something to say we are more likely to listen to what he is saying because of it. <br /> <br /> Also striking looks isnt Striking looks: Choice here. it is vague so it hits more people. So you dont have this tiny group that it applies to. It's not Striking looks: Hot mom. Where it would only hit a small group of people... it's Your looks are striking, People notice you because you are, Charming, beautiful, stunning, or Commanding, scary, or worthy of notice. <br /> You can be beautiful and scary at the same time...<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking Your character gets these bonuses.. Just like AWE gives you the bonuses. <br /> <br /> now you could give the +2 because the daughter is a knock out, but then give -3 because it's her dad... but consider the brady bunch.. Marsha was the &quot;hot one&quot; the middle daughter was always jealous because she felt that her sister got everything she wanted because she was pretty. It even applied to her parents. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:25:25-07:00","id":974462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974414#post974414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good read: <a href=\"http://www.newsweek.com/beauty-advantage-how-looks-affect-your-work-your-career-your-life-74313\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newsweek.com/beauty-advan...our-life-74313</a> <br /> good looking people make 4-5% more per year than the average joe... I would say that is a +1/+2 Bonus to their social rolls.<br /> <br /> But seriously guys. We are arguing about whether or not you should get a +1 or 2 bonus on your social rolls due to your looks? If you say that you cant get that bonus, what would the point of taking the merit be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit explicitly says to determine what the character looks like, how people react to those looks, and that depending on the particulars, the bonus might apply to a variety of different social rolls. Striking Looks is not &quot;you're pretty so you get +1 to +2 on any and all Social rolls.&quot; It's &quot;Your appearance is noteworthy in some way, so you get +1 to +2 on rolls where your appearance would be an advantage&quot;. So no, we're not arguing over whether or not you should get the bonus, we were arguing over what rolls the bonus should apply to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974414#post974414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the gay guy could be more easily persuaded by the pretty woman. it isnt about whether or not you are sexually attracted to them, it's about psychology saying that as people ( and vampires were people ) are more likely to listen to something we find visually appealing. More likely to consider their point of view, more likely to let them finish their thoughts. We might not be sexually attracted to Brad Pitt, but we could all agree that he is a good looking man. Does that mean we want to do him? no. It just means he is easy on the eyes and if he had something to say we are more likely to listen to what he is saying because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just about sexual attraction. It's not even just about looking good. It's about being <i>striking</i> in some way. That can be expressed in many different ways, and people will react to various striking looks in different ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974414#post974414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also striking looks isnt Striking looks: Choice here. it is vague so it hits more people. So you dont have this tiny group that it applies to. It's not Striking looks: Hot mom. Where it would only hit a small group of people... it's Your looks are striking, People notice you because you are, Charming, beautiful, stunning, or Commanding, scary, or worthy of notice. <br /> You can be beautiful and scary at the same time...<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking Your character gets these bonuses.. Just like AWE gives you the bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Metit explicitly says to determine what the character looks like and how people react to that. That doesn't mean it only applies to a small group, but it does mean that you do choose what it is about your appearance specifically that is striking, and to determine how people feel about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972274-odd-frenzy-question?p=974414#post974414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now you could give the +2 because the daughter is a knock out, but then give -3 because it's her dad...</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you <i>could</i>, but that's not how the Merit works. It gives bonuses to certain rolls, it doesn't give penalties. I would probably ask for more specific details about her appearance than &quot;a knockout&quot; but let's just assume she's &quot;conventionally pretty&quot; by a western standard. I'd probably say the +2 applies on most rolls to persuade most people, possibly including her parents, but it's going to depend on the specific circumstances. It'll probably help her charm her dad into letting her get away with little things (&quot;how can I stay mad at that face?&quot; and all that), but it's probably not going to help her convince him to let her go out alone at night. It almost definitely won't help her if for some reason she tries to seduce him into sex (although I wouldn't even allow a roll for that, it would just fail). It's not a question of <i>who</i> the bonus applies to, it's a question of <i>what rolls</i> it applies to, and who the subject of the roll is to the character is one of many factors that go into determining if the bonus should apply to a given roll or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T14:53:58-07:00","id":976738,"title":"","content":"I'd be reluctant to let Dominate OR Majesty help. The reason being that I see Majesty just as much as manipulation as Dominate and I view a touchstone bringing someone out of Frenzy to be an result of the vampire's empathy with the touchstone, not the touchstone being able to fast-talk them or something. A vampire's daughter calming them from their murderous rage isn't going to be made mire likely by their daughter being able to supernaturally charm people. In fact I think feeling they were being manipulated by someone they cared about would make them even angrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}